cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cambium in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Cambium: a self-organising growth model of silver birch, crown and roots"
authors:
  - alias: rar-file
version: 0.9.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/rar-file/cambium"
url: "https://rar-file.github.io/cambium/"
abstract: >-
  Cambium grows a tree year by year, crown and roots, from light, water and carbon: a self-organising
  model after Palubicki et al. (2009) with hydraulics, root growth by competition for soil water, wood
  mechanics and stand dynamics. The first species is silver birch (Betula pendula). It writes yearly
  statistics for science and game-ready meshes for real-time engines.
keywords:
  - tree growth model
  - functional-structural plant model
  - silver birch
  - Betula pendula
  - procedural generation
  - forest dynamics
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Self-organizing tree models for image synthesis"
    authors:
      - family-names: Palubicki
        given-names: Wojciech
      - family-names: Horel
